From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:38:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: CSG-scope in-stream sync signals when a VkQueue is
 one queue group

On kbase every in-stream sync signal used SYSTEM scope (csf-v11/077),
because each subqueue was its own CSG and a SYNC_WAIT on a sibling CSG is
only woken by a SYSTEM-scope update. A SYSTEM-scope update also interrupts
the host, so every render pass, barrier and ring-buffer release cost a GPU
interrupt and a wakeup of the kernel and of the threads polling it.

With one queue group per VkQueue (rg477m/004, the default) the subqueues
that wait on these signals share the signalling CSG, so CSG scope is enough.
Use it there. Signals another VkQueue may wait on (events) keep SYSTEM
scope, as does the per-submit queue signal the host waits on, and so does
PANVK_KBASE_ONE_GROUP=0. PANVK_SYSTEM_SCOPE_SIGNALS=1 restores the old scope.

drawbench, interrupts per frame: 64 independent passes 39.7 -> 3.1,
64 dependent passes 44 -> 3.0 (the stock Mali driver: about 2), 4-5% less
frame time. Tomb Raider (2013) benchmark: GPU interrupts 9093 -> 914 per
second, DXVK's queue thread 13.7% -> 4.1% of a core (stock: 4.1%), the
wrapper's swapchain thread 11.5% -> 2.3%, same frame rate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: D3D/Vulkan CPU overhead: in-stream sync signals between the subqueues of one VkQueue use CSG scope when the VkQueue is one kbase queue group (rg477m/004 default), so they no longer raise a GPU interrupt each; signals another VkQueue may wait on (events) and the per-submit queue signal keep SYSTEM scope
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: rg477m/004 (one queue group per VkQueue); applies after rg477m/047
Validation test: drawbench GPU interrupts per frame 39.7 -> 3.1 (independent passes), 44 -> 3.0 (dependent passes), frame time -4-5%; Tomb Raider (2013) benchmark, DXVK 1.11.1, quietd Stock, uncapped: interrupts 9093 -> 914/s, dxvk-queue thread 13.7% -> 4.1% of a core, swapchain thread 11.5% -> 2.3%, 73.4 vs 72.4 fps (same within run spread); Arkham City 10 rounds 36.5 vs 36.0 fps; PanProbe compat 38/38 x2; vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 suite 308 PASS, the one difference the known upstream test_sampler_border_color flake (B27); opt-out PANVK_SYSTEM_SCOPE_SIGNALS=1
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_instr.h        | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_event.c |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_instr.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_instr.h
index 34d20705..56fe7916 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_instr.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_instr.h
@@ -91,8 +91,32 @@ void panvk_per_arch(panvk_instr_end_work_async)(
    const struct panvk_instr_end_args *const args,
    struct cs_async_op ts_async_op);
 
+/* Scope for in-stream signals that only the other subqueues of the same
+ * VkQueue wait on. On kbase each subqueue used to be its own CSG, and a
+ * SYNC_WAIT on a sibling CSG is only woken by a SYSTEM-scope update, which
+ * also interrupts the host. With one queue group per VkQueue (rg477m/004,
+ * PANVK_KBASE_ONE_GROUP, the default) the waiters share the signalling CSG,
+ * so CSG scope wakes them without an interrupt per signal.
+ * PANVK_SYSTEM_SCOPE_SIGNALS=1 restores SYSTEM scope. */
 static inline enum mali_cs_sync_scope
 panvk_cs_signal_scope(const struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
+{
+   if (to_panvk_physical_device(cmdbuf->vk.base.device->physical)
+          ->kbase_node_path[0]) {
+      static int csg = -1;
+      if (csg < 0)
+         csg = !debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_SYSTEM_SCOPE_SIGNALS", false) &&
+               debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_KBASE_ONE_GROUP", true);
+      return csg ? MALI_CS_SYNC_SCOPE_CSG : MALI_CS_SYNC_SCOPE_SYSTEM;
+   }
+
+   return MALI_CS_SYNC_SCOPE_CSG;
+}
+
+/* Scope for signals another VkQueue (another queue group on kbase) may wait
+ * on, e.g. events: SYSTEM on kbase. */
+static inline enum mali_cs_sync_scope
+panvk_cs_signal_scope_cross_queue(const struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
 {
    if (to_panvk_physical_device(cmdbuf->vk.base.device->physical)
           ->kbase_node_path[0])
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_event.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_event.c
index c648beb1..f91c92c5 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_event.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_event.c
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ panvk_per_arch(CmdSetEvent2)(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer, VkEvent _event,
             }
 
             cs_move32_to(b, seqno, 1);
-            cs_sync32_set(b, false, panvk_cs_signal_scope(cmdbuf), seqno,
+            cs_sync32_set(b, false, panvk_cs_signal_scope_cross_queue(cmdbuf), seqno,
                           sync_addr, cs_defer(sb_mask | SB_MASK(DEFERRED_FLUSH),
                                               SB_ID(DEFERRED_SYNC)));
          }
